\begin{proposition}[A prescribed sequence]
\label{prop:ancient-sequence}
For every reference point $o$ and every prescribed sequence $\tau_i>0$
with $\tau_i\to\infty$, there are global minimizers $p_i$ of
$\ell_o(\cdot,\tau_i)$ with $\ell_o(p_i,\tau_i)\leq n/2$.
On the original carrier set
\[
 g_i(t)=\tau_i^{-1}g(\tau_i t),\quad
 R_i(t,x)=\tau_i R(\tau_i t,x),\quad
 A_i(t,x)=\tau_i A(\tau_i t,x),\qquad t<0.
\]
The construction retains the exact reference and scale sequence.
Monotonicity of the sequence is not required.
\lean{PoincareMT.ancientBlowupSequenceSetup}
\source{MT2007}
\dcref{Corollary 6.74, p. 142}
\dcref{Theorem 7.10 and Claim 7.11,
pp. 154--156}
\dcref{Theorem 9.11, pp. 183--185}
\uses{thm:ancient-structure}
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
On every finite backward interval, reduced-length coercivity gives a quadratic
distance lower bound. Completeness makes the reduced length proper, so its
continuous representative attains a minimum. The reduced-geometry minimum
estimate bounds it by $n/2$. Choose a minimizer at each prescribed time and
apply the displayed parabolic rescaling on the original carrier.
\end{proof}

